//window handles using iterator
Set<String> allWindows=driver.getwindowHandles();
Iterator it=allWindows.iterator();
while(it.hasNext())
{
  String currentWindow=it.next();
  driver.switchTo().window(currentWindow);
  System.out.println(driver.getTitle());
}
//windows handles using for each
Set<String> allWindows=driver.getwindowHandles();
Iterator it=allWindows.iterator();
for(String wind: it)
{
  driver.switchTo().window(wind);
  System.out.println(driver.getTitle());
}
//windows handles using for loop
Set<String> allWindows=driver.getwindowHandles();
List<WebElement> listWindows=new ArrayList<>(allWindows);
for(int i=0; i<listWindows.size(); i++)
{
  String currentWindow=listWindows.get(i);
  driver.switchTo().window(currentWindow);
}


 Basic Window Handle Questions
	1. What is a window handle in Selenium?
		○ A window handle is a unique string identifier for each open browser window or tab managed by the WebDriver.
	2. How do you get the window handle of the current window?
String currentWindow = driver.getWindowHandle();
	3. How do you get all window handles?
Set<String> allWindows = driver.getWindowHandles();
	4. How do you switch between windows using Selenium?
for (String handle : driver.getWindowHandles()) {
    driver.switchTo().window(handle);
}
Intermediate/Scenario-Based Questions
	1. How do you close only the child window and switch back to the parent?
String parentWindow = driver.getWindowHandle();
Set<String> allWindows = driver.getWindowHandles();

for (String window : allWindows) {
    if (!window.equals(parentWindow)) {
        driver.switchTo().window(window);
        driver.close();  // Close child window
    }
}

driver.switchTo().window(parentWindow);  // Back to parent
	2. How can you perform actions in a new tab or window opened after clicking a link?
		○ First click the link, then switch to the new window:
driver.findElement(By.linkText("Open Window")).click();
Set<String> handles = driver.getWindowHandles();

for (String handle : handles) {
    driver.switchTo().window(handle);
    if (!driver.getTitle().equals("Parent Window Title")) {
        break;
    }
}
	3. How do you ensure you're switching to the correct window?
		○ Use driver.getTitle() or driver.getCurrentUrl() to identify the right one:
for (String handle : driver.getWindowHandles()) {
    driver.switchTo().window(handle);
    if (driver.getTitle().contains("Expected Title")) {
        break;
    }
}
Advanced/Edge Cases
	1. What happens if you switch to a closed window?
		○ Selenium throws a NoSuchWindowException.
	2. How do you open a new tab using JavaScript?
JavascriptExecutor js = (JavascriptExecutor) driver;
js.executeScript("window.open()");
	3. Can you switch between tabs using keyboard shortcuts in Selenium?
		○ Yes, using the Robot class:
Robot robot = new Robot();
robot.keyPress(KeyEvent.VK_CONTROL);
robot.keyPress(KeyEvent.VK_TAB);
robot.keyRelease(KeyEvent.VK_TAB);
robot.keyRelease(KeyEvent.VK_CONTROL);
 Bonus: Common Mistakes
	• Forgetting to switch back to the original window.
	• Assuming order of getWindowHandles() – it returns a Set, which is unordered.
	• Using Thread.sleep() instead of WebDriverWait when waiting for the new window to open.





